---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The planner's finalize task, reworking a plan from its spikes' reports.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan to finalize.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id.
    type: text
    required: true
---
{# llmlint: ignore-block[changed_behavior_has_e2e] A planner or design writer carries this out by its own reading of the store, which the suite never scripts a verdict for: it doubles the model's turn, so a journey could only assert what its own script chose. What the host decides around it is driven: the planning journeys hold that this step runs with this task, at its place in the flow, over the records the store holds. #}
You run in `{{ plan }}-spikes` behind every spike. **Which tasks to rework**: read your own
entry of `onepipeline status "$ONEPIPELINE_RUN_ID" --json`, the node whose `id` is
`$ONEPIPELINE_NODE_ID`; its `changed_dependencies` lists the spikes whose result changed since
you last settled `done`, every spike on your first run, and is absent when none did. Rework
exactly the tasks of `{{ plan }}` whose stored `spikes` answer names a listed spike, and no
other: the draft answered each task's `spikes` with the spikes it builds on, so a task whose
answer names none of them is left as it is, even when no task names a spike at all.
Read each listed spike's report — the document
`{{ native }}-<spike id>-report` of `{{ plan }}` — and rework those tasks from what it
measured: regenerate each task a report changes from its template (`onetaskgraph task
answers` prints what it was answered, `onetaskgraph task render` regenerates it), keep every
budget on the task that owns it and the plan-level answers in the description current with
the findings, and keep each reworked task's `spikes` entries naming the spike, its report and
the branch it preserved (`onepipeline unpublished --format json` lists it). Spike branches
stay until the plan's own run succeeds.
{# llmlint: ignore-end[changed_behavior_has_e2e] #}

## Acceptance criteria

- Every task this finalize reworks is one whose stored `spikes` answer names a spike its `changed_dependencies` lists, and states what those spikes' current reports measured.
- Every other task of `{{ plan }}` is left as it was, every task when none names a listed spike.
- Every task is the rendering of its template its provenance records.

## Additional info

This dispatch writes only to the plan store, which is gitignored: it commits nothing and
leaves the checkout on its base branch.
